# Missing Marks Management System: Student API requests
# Requires the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Base URL matches the local backend default; change it if your server uses another port.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@studentEmail = student@example.test
@studentPassword = SET_TO_THE_SAME_VALUE_AS_DEMO_SEED_PASSWORD
# Get these IDs from Prisma Studio after seeding. The demo seed creates DEMO101,
# DEMO-PERIOD-2026 enrollment, but does not print the generated UUIDs.
@courseUnitId = SET_COURSE_UNIT_UUID
@academicPeriodId = SET_ACADEMIC_PERIOD_UUID
# Set these to records owned by the demo student for those endpoint-specific tests.
@rejectedReportId = SET_REJECTED_REPORT_UUID
@notificationId = SET_NOTIFICATION_UUID

### Setup
# In backend/, seed synthetic data with a non-production password of at least 12 chars:
# DEMO_SEED_PASSWORD='your-local-demo-password' npm run db:seed
# Then set @studentPassword above to that exact value. Obtain the DEMO101 unit and
# DEMO-PERIOD-2026 period IDs in Prisma Studio and replace the placeholders.
# Send Login first. The REST Client cookie jar should retain the access_token cookie
# for subsequent requests to the same host.

### Login as the seeded student
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}

### Authenticated user check (confirms login/cookie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 1. Get own student profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/profile

### 2. List own reports (first page)
# @name listReports
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/reports?page=1&limit=10

### 3. Submit a report (requires seeded enrollment IDs above)
# @name createReport
POST {{baseUrl}}/student/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseUnitId": "{{courseUnitId}}",
  "academicPeriodId": "{{academicPeriodId}}",
  "assessmentComponent": "CAT 1",
  "description": "Synthetic REST Client test: my CAT 1 mark is missing."
}

### 4. Get the report created by the previous request
# @name getCreatedReport
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}

### 5. List comments on the new report
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}/comments

### 6. Add a clarification to the new report
# @name addClarification
POST {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Synthetic clarification: I completed CAT 1 on the scheduled date."
}

### 7. Confirm your clarification is visible in the report thread
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}/comments

### 8. Edit the new report while its status is Submitted
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessmentComponent": "CAT 1 - corrected description",
  "description": "Synthetic REST Client test: please verify my CAT 1 mark."
}

### 9. Submit an appeal (requires an owned report with status REJECTED)
# Appeals are limited to one per report. The demo seed does not create a rejected report.
POST {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{rejectedReportId}}/appeals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Synthetic appeal test: please review the decision and supporting records.",
  "comments": "This is test data only."
}

### 10. Withdraw the new report while it is still Submitted
# Send this after testing report details, comments, and editing. It changes the report
# status to Withdrawn, so it cannot then be edited or used for an appeal.
POST {{baseUrl}}/student/reports/{{createReport.response.body.$.data.id}}/withdraw

### 11. Get own attendance history
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/attendance?page=1&limit=10

### 12. List own notifications
# @name listNotifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/notifications?page=1&limit=10

### 13. Mark one of your notifications as read
# First obtain a notification ID from listNotifications, then set @notificationId above.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/student/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
